---
// Side-by-side comparison of pprof heap profile views: alloc_space (GC churn) vs inuse_space (leaks).
const W = 900;
const H = 280;
---
<figure class="gpasi">
  <div class="gpasi-scroll">
    <svg viewBox={`0 0 ${W} ${H}`} role="img" aria-label="Comparison contrasting pprof -alloc_space which catches transient garbage generation versus -inuse_space which pinpoints live memory leaks.">
      {/* Left panel: alloc_space / alloc_objects */}
      <rect x="14" y="14" width="430" height="252" rx="10" class="gpasi-card" />
      <text x="30" y="42" class="gpasi-h">
        <tspan data-lang-en>1. -alloc_space / -alloc_objects: Finds GC Churn &amp; CPU Drag</tspan>
        <tspan data-lang-vi>1. -alloc_space / -alloc_objects: Săn Xả Rác GC &amp; Nghẽn CPU</tspan>
      </text>

      <rect x="30" y="60" width="398" height="68" rx="6" class="gpasi-box is-ok" />
      <text x="44" y="81" class="gpasi-code">go tool pprof -alloc_space mem.pprof</text>
      <text x="44" y="100" class="gpasi-m">
        <tspan data-lang-en>Cumulative bytes allocated (even if GC freed right after).</tspan>
        <tspan data-lang-vi>Tổng byte đã cấp từ đầu (kể cả rác vừa bị GC dọn ngay).</tspan>
      </text>

      <rect x="30" y="140" width="398" height="110" rx="6" class="gpasi-box" />
      <text x="44" y="162" class="gpasi-b">Use this when: p99 spikes &amp; CPU is high on GC</text>
      <text x="44" y="182" class="gpasi-m">- Spots short-lived JSON buffers &amp; fmt.Sprintf churn</text>
      <text x="44" y="201" class="gpasi-m">- Pair with -alloc_objects to catch tiny 16B allocs</text>
      <text x="44" y="220" class="gpasi-b-ok">- Directly cuts latency &amp; GC Mark Assist pauses</text>

      {/* Right panel: inuse_space / inuse_objects */}
      <rect x="460" y="14" width="426" height="252" rx="10" class="gpasi-card is-red" />
      <text x="476" y="42" class="gpasi-b-red">
        <tspan data-lang-en>2. -inuse_space (Default): Finds OOM Memory Leaks</tspan>
        <tspan data-lang-vi>2. -inuse_space (Mặc định): Săn Rò Rỉ RAM Gây OOMKill</tspan>
      </text>

      <rect x="476" y="60" width="394" height="68" rx="6" class="gpasi-box" />
      <text x="490" y="81" class="gpasi-code">go tool pprof -inuse_space -diff_base=t0.pb t1.pb</text>
      <text x="490" y="100" class="gpasi-m">
        <tspan data-lang-en>Shows ONLY bytes STILL alive right now after GC.</tspan>
        <tspan data-lang-vi>Chỉ tính RAM ĐANG SỐNG lúc chụp (chưa thu hồi được).</tspan>
      </text>

      <rect x="476" y="140" width="394" height="110" rx="6" class="gpasi-box" />
      <text x="490" y="162" class="gpasi-b-red">Use this when: RSS climbs toward Kubernetes OOM</text>
      <text x="490" y="182" class="gpasi-m">- Spots unbounded caches, leaked slices, stuck maps</text>
      <text x="490" y="201" class="gpasi-m">- Sample rate: 1 per 512 KB (runtime.MemProfileRate)</text>
      <text x="490" y="220" class="gpasi-b">- Diff t1 vs t0 via -diff_base to pinpoint leak root</text>
    </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption>
    <span data-lang-en>Choosing -alloc_space vs -inuse_space decides what problem you see: short-lived garbage bursts vanish from inuse_space immediately yet dominate alloc_space, whereas slow unbounded cache leaks shine cleanly inside -inuse_space -diff_base.</span>
    <span data-lang-vi>Chọn sai góc nhìn trên Heap profile rất dễ bỏ lọt bệnh: rác sinh rồi chết ngay biến mất khỏi inuse_space nhưng phình to trong alloc_space; ngược lại rò rỉ cache làm OOM lộ rõ qua inuse_space kèm -diff_base.</span>
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .gpasi { margin: 2em 0; width: 100%; }
  .gpasi-scroll { overflow-x: auto; }
  .gpasi svg { display: block; width: 100%; min-width: 680px; height: auto; }
  .gpasi text { font-size: 12px; fill: var(--text-body); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .gpasi-card { fill: var(--bg-alt); stroke: var(--border); stroke-width: 1.5; }
  .gpasi-card.is-red { stroke: var(--red); fill: var(--red-tint-bg); }
  .gpasi-box { fill: var(--bg); stroke: var(--border); stroke-width: 1.2; }
  .gpasi-box.is-ok { stroke: rgb(21, 128, 61); }
  :global(html[data-theme='dark']) .gpasi-box.is-ok { stroke: rgb(74, 222, 128); }
  .gpasi-h { font-size: 14px; font-weight: 700; fill: var(--text); }
  .gpasi-b { font-weight: 700; fill: var(--text); }
  .gpasi-b-red { font-weight: 700; fill: var(--red); }
  .gpasi-b-ok { font-weight: 700; fill: rgb(21, 128, 61); }
  :global(html[data-theme='dark']) .gpasi-b-ok { fill: rgb(74, 222, 128); }
  .gpasi-code { font-family: var(--font-mono, ui-monospace, monospace); font-size: 11px; fill: var(--text); }
  .gpasi-m { fill: var(--text-muted); font-size: 11px; }
  .gpasi figcaption { margin-top: 10px; font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.55; text-align: center; }
</style>
